# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
# BusyBox 1.38.0 for the baseline ROOTFS: `make defconfig`, then these lines win (build.sh replaces each
# symbol's line, runs oldconfig, and fails if a value did not stick). Goal: every applet that can build
# static and can work on the board; out only what cannot work there:
#   PAM, SELinux             no such libraries/policies in a static musl/glibc userspace
#   NFS / CIFS mount helpers no RPC/CIFS userspace or kernel client in the baseline
#   TC, HWCLOCK              do not build: tc.c against 7.x headers (TCA_CBQ_MAX), hwclock.c against
#                            musl 1.2 time64 (SYS_settimeofday). Measured by the C2Air session with the
#                            same 1.38.0 (c2air docs/userspace-spec.md); LIVI's busybox.sed drops TC too.
# "udev helpers": BusyBox has no udev applets; mdev is built but never registered as the hotplug helper
# (nothing may autoload radio modules), so nothing else is excluded under that heading.
# Additions over defconfig: static, the MTD/UBI tools (flash_erase itself is not a BusyBox applet: see
# the mtd-utils recipe). The VT/console applets LIVI's busybox.sed removes are KEPT (they build; the
# owner rule is "exclude only what cannot work"); drop them here if the rootfs ever gets tight.
CONFIG_STATIC=y
# CONFIG_PAM is not set
# CONFIG_SELINUX is not set
# CONFIG_FEATURE_MOUNT_NFS is not set
# CONFIG_FEATURE_MOUNT_CIFS is not set
# CONFIG_FEATURE_INETD_RPC is not set
# CONFIG_TC is not set
# CONFIG_FEATURE_TC_INGRESS is not set
# CONFIG_HWCLOCK is not set
CONFIG_FLASHCP=y
CONFIG_FLASH_ERASEALL=y
CONFIG_FLASH_LOCK=y
CONFIG_FLASH_UNLOCK=y
CONFIG_NANDWRITE=y
CONFIG_NANDDUMP=y
CONFIG_UBIATTACH=y
CONFIG_UBIDETACH=y
CONFIG_UBIMKVOL=y
CONFIG_UBIRMVOL=y
CONFIG_UBIRSVOL=y
CONFIG_UBIUPDATEVOL=y
CONFIG_UBIRENAME=y
CONFIG_DEVMEM=y
CONFIG_I2CGET=y
CONFIG_I2CSET=y
CONFIG_I2CDUMP=y
CONFIG_I2CDETECT=y
CONFIG_I2CTRANSFER=y
CONFIG_MODPROBE=y
CONFIG_DEPMOD=y
CONFIG_MOUNTPOINT=y
CONFIG_READLINK=y
CONFIG_FEATURE_READLINK_FOLLOW=y
CONFIG_CTTYHACK=y
CONFIG_TAR=y
CONFIG_FEATURE_TAR_CREATE=y
